{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 29, "model_name": "nvidia/llama-3.3-nemotron-super-49b-v1", "content": "I woke up to the same old alarm blaring in my ear, or so I thought. As I reached over to turn it off, I noticed something was off. The room seemed... pixelated. At first, I brushed it off as a side effect of not getting enough sleep, but as I got out of bed and started my morning routine, the feeling persisted. Every movement I made felt slightly delayed, like there was a fraction of a second lag between my brain and my body. And then I saw it - a health bar hovering above my head, slowly replenishing as I brushed my teeth.\n\n***\n\nPanic set in as I stumbled through my apartment, searching for answers. Every object I interacted with had a subtle highlight effect, and I could see experience points ticking up in the corner of my vision whenever I completed a mundane task, like making breakfast. I felt like a character in one of the RPGs I used to play obsessively. But how? And why? I approached the window, hesitating for a moment before pulling back the curtain. The city outside was familiar yet strange, with NPCs going about their daily business, completely oblivious to my newfound awareness. I had to find a way out, or at least understand the rules of this bizarre new reality. But for now, I just stood there, frozen, as the game continued to play on around me.", "logprobs": [{"token": "I", "logprob": -1.3680917024612427}, {"token": " woke", "logprob": -0.11377966403961182}, {"token": " up", "logprob": -1.9192511899746023e-05}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -4.6967357775429264e-05}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.14508870244026184}, {"token": " same", "logprob": -0.780907392501831}, {"token": " old", "logprob": -1.4322179555892944}, {"token": " alarm", "logprob": -0.12031585723161697}, {"token": " bl", "logprob": -0.20561963319778442}, {"token": "aring", "logprob": -0.02631078101694584}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -7.390948667307384e-06},